course: dictionary
lesson: 9229
title: Son: one word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A son is a boy or man who is someone's child. A girl who is someone's child is a daughter. The plural of son is sons. Most of the time, son means a child, as in «Darwin and his son experimented on grass seedlings in the 1880s.» Here, son is Darwin's child.
explain: Look at the words around the word to see which meaning is used. Sometimes an older man says «Thanks, son» to a boy who is not his child. He is being friendly. The clue is that he is older and the boy is not his own child.
explain: Some phrases use son in a fixed way. «Only son» means the one son in a family. «Eldest son» means the first son born. «Father and son» means a father and his son together. When you meet a phrase, read the whole phrase, not just the word son.
fact: A son is a boy or man who is someone's child.
fact: The plural of son is sons.
fact: «Son» can be a friendly word an older man uses to a boy.
fact: In a family, a son and a daughter are brother and sister.
fact: «Eldest son» means the first son born in a family.
exercise: In «Harry's son Archie», who is Archie to Harry? | Harry's friend from school | Harry's father | *Harry's child, a boy | A king
exercise: In «Darwin and his son experimented on grass seedlings», what does son mean? | *A boy or man who is Darwin's child | A plant that grows in the shade | A type of cheese | A friendly word for a boy
exercise: An older man in a shop says, «Thanks, son.» What does son show? | He is cross and wants the boy to leave | He is a king | *He is being friendly to a boy | He is the boy's father
test: Which phrase means the first son born in a family? | Sons | *Eldest son | Only son | Father and son
test: In a story, what is a king's son called? | A farmer | A sailor | *A prince | A duke
exam: In «Isaac's son Jacob tricked his twin Esau», what is Jacob to Isaac? | *Isaac's child | Isaac's teacher | A king | Isaac's brother
